course: dictionary
lesson: 16037
title: A trace of the past
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A vestige is a small part or trace left over from something that used to be bigger or used to exist. «Only a vestige of the old wall was left after the storm.» Most of the wall had gone, but a small piece was still there. So a vestige is what remains.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Words like «left», «last» or «remains» often sit near a vestige, because it is something left behind. Then swap in «a tiny trace» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Scientists use the word too. A vestigial body part has lost most of its old job. «Some whales have tiny leg bones inside their bodies, vestiges of legs their ancestors once used.» Those bones are small and no longer do the job they once did.
fact: A vestige is a small trace left of something that used to be bigger or used to exist.
fact: «The last vestiges of the castle» means the last small bits still standing.
fact: «Not a vestige of» means «not even a little».
fact: A vestigial body part has lost most of its old use, like the tiny leg bones inside some whales.
fact: The human tailbone is a vestigial part, a left-over from our distant past.
exercise: «Only a vestige of the old wall was left after the storm.» What is a vestige? | A brand new wall | A loud noise | *A small trace left of something bigger | A huge storm cloud
exercise: «There was not a vestige of cake left on the plate.» What does not a vestige of mean? | *Not even a little | A large slice | Plenty for everyone | A sweet smell
exercise: Which part of a whale is a vestigial body part? | Its spout | *Its tiny leg bones inside its body | Its tail fin | Its blowhole
test: «The house was gone, but a vestige of its garden fence still stood.» What was still standing? | The whole house | The garden gate in full | *A small part of the fence | A new shed
test: Vestigial means: | Brand new and shiny | Very large and strong | *Having lost most of its old use | Full of colour
exam: Which word means a small trace left behind? | Vestment | Vestibule | *Vestige | Vessel
